{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7EbMZoU2cSrXtuhBN81","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I write it, a few questions. Your answers will change what the page says:\n\n1. **What do you do for salons that a general bookkeeper doesn't?** For example: tips, commission or tiered pay, booth renters vs. employees, taxable retail sales vs. non-taxable services, or the reports from your clients' booking systems. This will probably be the core of the page, so concrete examples help most.\n2. **Who's the main reader?** Is it an owner doing their own books at midnight, one leaving another bookkeeper, or one whose accountant keeps sending everything back? I'll write the opening for that person.\n3. **Should the page mention the price increase and the three missed closes?** I'd suggest one short line on each, said plainly. For example: \"the 10th, every month (I missed it three times last year, and told those clients ahead of time).\" If that's true, the honesty builds trust. Is it fine to include them, and what actually happened when you missed?\n4. **What name and location should I use?** Give me your name or business name, plus the state or area you serve. Sales tax rules depend on the state, so naming yours tells the reader you know their rules.\n5. **What happens on the 20-minute call, and when can people book it?** For example: do you look at their current books, and do you give them a yes/no on fit? Also, what should the button say, if you have a preference?\n\nIf you don't know or don't want to share something, just say so and I'll leave it out instead of guessing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":9521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":678},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"sta